WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.290 --> 00:00:07.940
These villagers thought they were safe after
escaping the tsunami that tore through the

00:00:07.940 --> 00:00:10.170
western coast of Java.

00:00:10.170 --> 00:00:18.930
But now that they've returned, they face a
new problem.

00:00:18.930 --> 00:00:22.720
Around 6 in the morning, the water began rising.

00:00:22.720 --> 00:00:27.500
I went out to get some food, and when I came
back, the water was almost chest high.

00:00:27.500 --> 00:00:32.850
Our village has never been flooded like this.

00:00:32.850 --> 00:00:37.250
Johnny moved his family because of the chance
of another tsunami.

00:00:37.250 --> 00:00:44.010
In this home behind me he lives with 25 others.

00:00:44.010 --> 00:00:50.890
It’s a tight squeeze, he says, but at least
they are living among family members, they’re

00:00:50.890 --> 00:00:52.190
all accounted for and alive.

00:00:52.190 --> 00:00:58.380
All his has now is his faith and his family.

00:00:58.380 --> 00:01:05.239
Johnny's wife Maesaroh remembers the moment
she had to leave.

00:01:05.239 --> 00:01:10.030
When I heard talk of a second tsunami coming,
I grabbed my children and ran to my sister’s

00:01:10.030 --> 00:01:11.030
house.

00:01:11.030 --> 00:01:13.500
People were panicking and fleeing, screaming,
'Run!

00:01:13.500 --> 00:01:15.170
Run!' because the wave was coming.

00:01:15.170 --> 00:01:20.470
I couldn’t think of anything else, the safety
of my children was my only priority.

00:01:20.470 --> 00:01:23.280
My youngest children are 8 and 3 years old.

00:01:23.280 --> 00:01:30.070
They're in a bit of a shock and have trouble
sleeping.

00:01:30.070 --> 00:01:35.560
So while the tsunami spared this family, the
floods still threaten their lives.

